{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788116261,"nonce":"744Zfjm3fI0rVebGkbUsMS/SO0U=","message":"ORCHESTRATOR VERIFICATION — spike 0.1. Branch merged; one acceptance line open.\n\nMerged `spec/0.1-profile-spike` to main as a **fast-forward** (26b638c..57263e7).\nNo assemblies in the range, so no `Build:` commit is owed. I added one commit of\nmy own before merging, 57263e7 (below).\n\n\n**1. Bench boots to a playable map, full v1 modlist, zero red errors — PASS.**\n\nThe worker's Player.log was no longer on disk, so its evidence was not\ncheckable; I booted the bench myself instead.\n\n    ./profile/make-profile-agent.sh          # idempotent: 32 mods, 1 missing (AutoRimmer, per 1.1)\n    cd ../_RimWorld-Agent \u0026\u0026 ./run-agent.sh --quicktest --fps 30\n\n    Mono path[0] = '/home/dorian/projects/rimworld/_RimWorld-Agent/RimWorldLinux_Data/Managed'\n      -\u003e isolation confirmed; the de-rooting fix works, the game is NOT rooted at Steam\n\n    ModsConfig.xml: activeMods 38 (unique 38), knownExpansions 6, version 1.6.4871\n    status.json:   gameLoaded:true, speed Normal, fps 30.0067\n    ticks: 96 @18:51:32 -\u003e 1475 @18:51:55 -\u003e 3847 @18:52:34  = 60.8 tps sustained\n    LogRelay relay.jsonl: 0 errors, 9 warnings  (exactly the FINDINGS section 5 set)\n    Player.log: 0 occurrences of Exception\n\nThe 9 warnings are the documented benign set, with the four Hospitality\ntutor-key entries correctly absent on a non-first boot — precisely as FINDINGS\npredicted.\n\n**2. Both display modes demonstrated, script-flagged — HALF. This is the one\nopen line.**\n\nSpecial-workspace mode verified live by me while the bench ran:\n\n    hyprctl clients  -\u003e class RimWorldLinux, workspace special:rwagent, hidden:False\n    hyprctl activewindow -\u003e localsend    (focus never moved)\n    fps 30.0 with the window hidden      (the render_unfocused fix works)\n\nXvfb mode: implemented and flagged (`--xvfb`, `--vnc`), documented with exact\ncommands, but never executed — `xorg-server-xvfb`/`x11vnc` are still not\ninstalled and sudo needs a password. Checked again at merge time; still absent.\n\n**3. FINDINGS.md committed with tps table, thermals + cap, per-frame set,\nbatchmode verdict, modlist deviations — PASS.**\n\nI re-derived the numbers from the raw artifacts rather than trusting the table:\n\n- 1026 samples in `scratch-spike/tps.ndjson` across 8 phases. Recomputed:\n  Normal 60.0 flat; Fast avg 180.0; Superfast avg 473.9 (claimed 472);\n  Ultrafast avg 891.8 med 899 max 920 (claimed avg 890); usb avg 561.7 max 1913\n  (claimed 567); budget-25@60 avg 1271.7 med 1481 (claimed 1267/1481);\n  budget-40 avg 1471.3 med 1573 (claimed 1467/1576); budget-25@30 avg 1386.9\n  med 1392 (claimed 1392/1381). Every row reproduces within a few tps; the\n  small gaps are sample-window choices, and no conclusion moves.\n- 239 thermal samples: Tctl min 80.8 / median 93.4 / max 94.1, cpu fan max 5700.\n  185 of 239 samples at or above 93C, 31 at or above 94C, **zero at or above\n  95C**. The plateau claim and the 1C-headroom claim both hold.\n- Per-frame update set (section 9) checked line by line against decompiled\n  `Game.UpdatePlay` and `Map.MapUpdate`: correct, in order, including the\n  `DrawingMap \u0026\u0026 CurrentMap == this` gate on the draw half. The load-bearing\n  consequence — `GameComponentUpdate` runs after the frame's MapUpdates, so a\n  yielding loop inherits vanilla's correctness envelope — is sound.\n\nTwo small overstatements, neither consequential: batchmode frame rate is\ndescribed as \"~2860 fps\" where the samples median ~2100 (max 3162), and the\nthermal minimum is given as 82.5 against a measured 80.8.\n\n\n`make-profile-agent.sh` linked `Mods/AutoRimmer` at `autorimmer/Mod`. Spec 1.1\nowns where that mod lives and states its layout root-relative — About/,\nSource/AutoRimmer/, Assemblies/ — matching every sibling repo (analyzerbridge,\nlogrelay, Factions all put those at the repo root beside their docs, and\n_RimWorld-Test links repo roots directly). Left as-is, 1.1's own stated paths\nwould have been wrong at the bench. Repointed at the repo root, one line, so\n1.1's worker inherits a profile that expects the layout its spec describes.\n\n\nAll three resolved by the worker on-issue with rationale (comments #2-#4):\nbench path + profile layout/flags, UltraSpeedBoost reachability, fps caps. I\nagree with all three; the UltraSpeedBoost one in particular does the right\nthing by answering \"yes, reachable\" and then arguing not to use it.\n\n\nAcceptance criteria are the definition of done, and \"both display modes\ndemonstrated\" is half-met. The remainder is not work — it is one package\ninstall that needs Dorian's password, then a 3-minute run:\n\n    sudo pacman -S --needed xorg-server-xvfb x11vnc\n    cd _RimWorld-Agent \u0026\u0026 ./run-agent.sh --xvfb --vnc --quicktest\n\nBLOCKED on that install. Set back to `state:next`: everything else is merged\nand every downstream spec has its amendment, so this is a short finish whenever\nthe package exists — or Dorian waives the line and it closes immediately.","files":null}]}